diff -aruN openssh-portable/BUFFER_CHECKER_FIX.md openssh-portable-fuzz-with-msg-gen-lib/BUFFER_CHECKER_FIX.md
--- openssh-portable/BUFFER_CHECKER_FIX.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ openssh-portable-fuzz-with-msg-gen-lib/BUFFER_CHECKER_FIX.md	2025-12-22 20:56:39.292985000 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,195 @@
+# Fix for Missing libbuffer_check.so and libmsg_generator Libraries
+
+## Problem
+
+When building openssh-portable with custom buffer checking libraries, the build fails with:
+
+```
+monitor.c:102:10: fatal error: 'msg_generator.h' file not found
+```
+
+And/or runtime errors:
+```
+libbuffer_check.so => not found (0)
+```
+
+## Root Cause
+
+The build system needs to:
+1. Include the buffer checker headers during compilation (`-I` flag)
+2. Link against the buffer checker libraries (`-l` flags)
+3. Add the library directory to the linker search path (`-L` flag)
+4. Embed the runtime library path in the binaries (`-Wl,-rpath`)
+
+## Solution
+
+Modify `Makefile.in` to add the buffer checker paths and libraries.
+
+### Changes Made to Makefile.in
+
+#### 1. Add BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT Variable (Line 53)
+```makefile
+BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT ?= /home/share/ptr_checker
+```
+
+This uses the `BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT` environment variable if set, otherwise defaults to `/home/share/ptr_checker`.
+
+#### 2. Add Include Path to CPPFLAGS (Line 54)
+```makefile
+CPPFLAGS=-I. -I$(srcdir) @CPPFLAGS@ -I$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT) $(PATHS) @DEFS@
+```
+
+This adds `-I$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT)` so the compiler can find `msg_generator.h` and `buffer_check_lib.h`.
+
+#### 3. Add Libraries to SSHDLIBS (Line 60)
+```makefile
+SSHDLIBS=@SSHDLIBS@ -lmsg_generator -lbuffer_check
+```
+
+This adds `-lmsg_generator -lbuffer_check` to link the required libraries.
+
+#### 4. Add Library Path and RPATH to LDFLAGS (Lines 70-71)
+```makefile
+LDFLAGS=-L. -Lopenbsd-compat/ -L$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT) -Wl,-rpath,$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT) @LDFLAGS@
+LDFLAGS_NOPIE=-L. -Lopenbsd-compat/ -L$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT) -Wl,-rpath,$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT) @LDFLAGS_NOPIE@
+```
+
+This:
+- Adds `-L$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT)` so the linker can find the libraries during build
+- Adds `-Wl,-rpath,$(BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT)` so the runtime linker can find the libraries when running the binary
+
+## Commands Run
+
+### 1. Navigate to openssh directory
+```bash
+cd /home/share/openssh-portable-fuzz
+# Or using pwd:
+cd $(pwd)
+```
+
+### 2. Edit Makefile.in
+```bash
+# Edit lines 53-54, 60, and 70-71 in Makefile.in with the changes above
+vi Makefile.in
+```
+
+### 3. Regenerate Makefile from Makefile.in
+```bash
+./config.status Makefile
+```
+
+### 4. Clean and Rebuild
+```bash
+make clean && make
+```
+
+### 5. Verify the Fix
+```bash
+ldd ./sshd
+```
+
+Expected output should show:
+```
+libbuffer_check.so => /home/share/ptr_checker/libbuffer_check.so (0x...)
+```
+
+No "not found" errors.
+
+## How to Reproduce
+
+### Method 1: Using config.status (if you already ran configure)
+```bash
+# 1. Copy the modified Makefile.in to your openssh source directory
+cp Makefile.in $(pwd)/
+
+# 2. Regenerate Makefile
+cd $(pwd)
+./config.status Makefile
+
+# 3. Build
+make clean && make
+```
+
+### Method 2: Using configure (fresh setup)
+```bash
+# 1. Navigate to openssh directory
+cd $(pwd)
+
+# 2. Copy the modified Makefile.in (if needed)
+# cp /path/to/modified/Makefile.in ./
+
+# 2. Run configure with your options
+./configure --with-kerberos5 --with-pam \
+    --prefix=$HOME/openssh-portable-fuzz \
+    --sbindir=$HOME/openssh-portable-fuzz \
+    --libexecdir=$HOME/openssh-portable-fuzz \
+    --sysconfdir=$HOME/openssh-portable-fuzz \
+    CFLAGS='-O0 -g' \
+    CC=afl-clang-lto
+
+# 3. Build
+make clean && make
+```
+
+## Environment Variable Override
+
+If you want to use a different path for the buffer checker libraries:
+
+```bash
+export BUFFER_CHECKER_ROOT=/your/custom/path
+./config.status Makefile
+make clean && make
+```
+
+The `?=` operator in Makefile.in means it will use the environment variable if set.
+
+## Verification
+
+After building, verify all libraries are found:
+
+```bash
+# Check sshd
+ldd ./sshd | grep -E "(buffer_check|msg_generator|not found)"
+
+# Check sshd-session
+ldd ./sshd-session | grep -E "(buffer_check|msg_generator|not found)"
+
+# Check sshd-auth
+ldd ./sshd-auth | grep -E "(buffer_check|msg_generator|not found)"
+```
+
+All should show the libraries pointing to the correct path, with no "not found" errors.
+
+## Files Modified
+
+- `Makefile.in` - Build system template (4 sections modified)
+
+## Files Generated
+
+- `Makefile` - Generated from Makefile.in by configure/config.status
+
+## Notes
+
+- The changes to `Makefile.in` are **permanent** and will persist across configure runs
+- The `Makefile` is **generated** and will be overwritten each time you run configure
+- Always edit `Makefile.in`, never edit `Makefile` directly
+- The `?=` operator in Make means "assign if not already defined", allowing environment variable override
+
+## Quick Reference: All Commands in Order
+
+```bash
+# Navigate to openssh directory
+cd /home/share/openssh-portable-fuzz
+
+# Edit Makefile.in (apply the 4 changes described above)
+vi Makefile.in
+
+# Regenerate Makefile
+./config.status Makefile
+
+# Clean and build
+make clean && make
+
+# Verify
+ldd ./sshd | grep buffer_check
+```
